-- Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 (Cth), first reading print (Senate),
-- 7 September 2026 (file 26S2721).
-- Part 4 -- Miscellaneous (ss 14-16).
--
-- Imports Part 2 (which brings Parts 1 and 3) and the Public Service Act 1999 s 39 boundary.

IMPORT `part2-selection`
IMPORT `psa-1999-s39`

§ `15 Appointments to which this Act applies`

-- s 15: "This Act applies in relation an appointment made on or after the commencement of this
-- section if the term of the appointment starts at least 12 months after that commencement."
-- (The print omits "to" after "in relation": ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-03.)
-- Commencement is at the start of the day after the Royal Assent (s 2; Acts Interpretation Act
-- s 3). Twelve months from the start of that day end immediately before the corresponding day
-- 12 months later, or at the end of that month if there is none (Acts Interpretation Act
-- s 2G(2)); a term "starts at least 12 months after that commencement" if it starts on or after
-- the first day after those 12 months.
@ref s 15; s 2(1); Acts Interpretation Act 1901 ss 2G(2), 3
GIVEN w IS A World
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first day a term may start for s 15 to apply, in` w MEANS
    `the first day after a period of` 12 `months starting on` (`the day this Act commences` w)

@ref s 15
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies in relation to` a `in` w IF
        a's `made on` AT LEAST `the day this Act commences` w
    AND a's `term starts on` AT LEAST `the first day a term may start for s 15 to apply, in` w

-- FORK-15, reading A (taken): s 15 speaks only of appointments. An acting arrangement is not an
-- appointment (s 11(3) keeps the chargé d'affaires out of s 9), so the Act applies to every
-- arrangement made on or after commencement.
@ref s 15; s 11; s 14(4)
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies in relation to the arrangement` x `in` w IF
    x's `made on` AT LEAST `the day this Act commences` w

-- FORK-15, reading B: an acting arrangement is an "appointment" for s 15, so the Act applies to it
-- only if the acting starts at least 12 months after commencement (taken as the day it is made).
@ref s 15; s 11
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies in relation to the arrangement, reading B of FORK-15,` x `in` w IF
        x's `made on` AT LEAST `the day this Act commences` w
    AND x's `made on` AT LEAST `the first day a term may start for s 15 to apply, in` w

§ `14 Overarching prohibition and consequences of non-compliance`

§§ `14(1) to (3) Appointments`

-- s 14(1): "An appointment to a designated diplomatic office must not be made otherwise than in
-- accordance with this Act."
-- FORK-16, reading A (taken): an appointment is made in accordance with the Act when s 9(1)
-- permits it. Defects in the process that led to it (a late or over-long list, a late notice, a
-- Committee established while another existed) are breaches of ss 10 and 12 by whoever owed
-- those duties, but do not make the appointment one made "otherwise than in accordance with this
-- Act". A Committee decision not made at a quorate meeting is not a recommendation at all
-- (part2-selection.l4), so it fails s 9(2) on either reading.
-- Where the Act does not apply in relation to the appointment (s 15), or the office is not a
-- designated diplomatic office, nothing in it is breached.
@ref s 14(1); s 9(1); s 15
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment` a `was made in accordance with this Act, in` w IF
        (NOT `is a designated diplomatic office` (a's `office`))
     OR (NOT `this Act applies in relation to` a `in` w)
     OR `section 9(1) permits` a

-- The process requirements for one Committee: established under s 12(1) and (8), members under
-- s 12(3)-(5), the list under s 10(1), (2) and (6), and the notice under s 10(3).
@ref ss 10, 12
GIVEN c   IS A `Selection Committee`
      all IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
      w   IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `among` all `was run in accordance with ss 10 and 12, in` w IF
        `the Committee` c `was established in accordance with s 12, beside` all
    AND `the Committee's membership complies with s 12(3) to (5)` c
    AND `the Minister complied with s 10(1) and (2) for` c `after` all `in` w
    AND ((NOT c's `notice given`) OR `the Committee` c `gave its notice in time in` w)

GIVEN cs  IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
      all IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
      w   IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every Committee in` cs `among` all `was run in accordance with ss 10 and 12, in` w MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            `the Committee` c `among` all `was run in accordance with ss 10 and 12, in` w
        AND `every Committee in` rest `among` all `was run in accordance with ss 10 and 12, in` w

-- FORK-16, reading B: "in accordance with this Act" takes in the whole process for the
-- appointment: every Committee for it must have been established, constituted, given its list and
-- given its notice as ss 10 and 12 require.
@ref s 14(1); ss 9, 10, 12
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment` a `was made in accordance with this Act, reading B of FORK-16, in` w IF
        `the appointment` a `was made in accordance with this Act, in` w
    AND (   (NOT `is a designated diplomatic office` (a's `office`))
         OR (NOT `this Act applies in relation to` a `in` w)
         OR `every Committee in` cs `among` cs `was run in accordance with ss 10 and 12, in` w)
    WHERE
        cs MEANS `the Committees for this appointment` a

-- s 14(2): "A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not affect the validity of the
-- appointment."
@ref s 14(2)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment` a `is invalid because of a failure to comply with s 14(1), in` w IF FALSE

-- Whether the appointment can take effect at all: Public Service Act 1999 s 39(1), which s 14(2)
-- does not displace (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-11).
@ref Public Service Act 1999 s 39(1); s 14(2)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Service Act 1999 s 39(1) lets take effect the appointment` a IF
    `section 39(1) lets the appointment take effect` (a's `made by the Governor-General`) (`is the office of a Head of Mission` (a's `office`)) (a's `appointee`'s `is an APS employee`)

-- s 14(3): "However, an appointment must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister
-- becomes aware of any failure to comply with subsection (1) in relation to the appointment."
-- The Bill does not say who terminates, or under what power (REF-30). Whether the Minister is
-- aware of the facts, and whether a termination came as soon as practicable, are facts.
@ref s 14(3)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment` a `must be terminated under s 14(3), in` w IF
        (NOT `the appointment` a `was made in accordance with this Act, in` w)
    AND a's `the Minister is aware of the facts of any failure to comply`

@ref s 14(3)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment` a `must be terminated under s 14(3), reading B of FORK-16, in` w IF
        (NOT `the appointment` a `was made in accordance with this Act, reading B of FORK-16, in` w)
    AND a's `the Minister is aware of the facts of any failure to comply`

@ref s 14(3)
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(3) has been complied with for` a `in` w IF
        (NOT `the appointment` a `must be terminated under s 14(3), in` w)
     OR a's `terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister became aware`

§§ `14(4) to (6) Chargé d'affaires`

-- s 14(4): "An arrangement for a person to act in a designated diplomatic office must not be made
-- otherwise than in accordance with this Act."
-- The Act's only requirement of an arrangement is s 11(2), which applies where s 11(1) does. An
-- arrangement to act on no occasion s 11(1) names meets no requirement of the Act and breaches
-- none (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-16). FORK-14 and FORK-15, readings A.
@ref s 14(4); s 11
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrangement` x `was made in accordance with this Act, in` w IF
        (NOT `is a designated diplomatic office` (x's `office`))
     OR (NOT `this Act applies in relation to the arrangement` x `in` w)
     OR (NOT `section 11 applies to` x)
     OR `section 11(2) is met for` x

-- s 14(5): "A failure to comply with subsection (4) does not affect the validity of the
-- arrangement."
@ref s 14(5)
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrangement` x `is invalid because of a failure to comply with s 14(4), in` w IF FALSE

-- s 14(6): "However, an arrangement must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister
-- becomes aware of any failure to comply with subsection (4) in relation to the arrangement."
@ref s 14(6)
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrangement` x `must be terminated under s 14(6), in` w IF
        (NOT `the arrangement` x `was made in accordance with this Act, in` w)
    AND x's `the Minister is aware of the facts of any failure to comply`

-- FORK-14, reading B: s 11(2) runs for as long as the person acts, so an arrangement must be
-- terminated once the chargé d'affaires comes to have an affiliation on day d and the Minister
-- knows of it.
@ref s 14(4), (6); s 11(2)
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`, w IS A World, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrangement` x `must be terminated under s 14(6), reading B of FORK-14, in` w `on` d IF
        `is a designated diplomatic office` (x's `office`)
    AND `this Act applies in relation to the arrangement` x `in` w
    AND `section 11 applies to` x
    AND (NOT `section 11(2) is met, reading B of FORK-14, for` x `on` d)
    AND x's `the Minister is aware of the facts of any failure to comply`

-- FORK-15, reading B, at the level of s 14(4).
@ref s 14(4); s 15
GIVEN x IS AN `acting arrangement`, w IS A World
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrangement` x `was made in accordance with this Act, reading B of FORK-15, in` w IF
        (NOT `is a designated diplomatic office` (x's `office`))
     OR (NOT `this Act applies in relation to the arrangement, reading B of FORK-15,` x `in` w)
     OR (NOT `section 11 applies to` x)
     OR `section 11(2) is met for` x

§§ `14(7) Commonwealth powers`

-- s 14(7): "Nothing in subsections (3) and (6) limit a power of the Commonwealth to terminate an
-- appointment or arrangement otherwise than under those subsections."
-- An appointment or arrangement may be ended under another power whether or not s 14(3) or (6)
-- requires it; the other power and its exercise are facts (REF-30).
@ref s 14(7)
GIVEN `terminated under another power of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsections 14(3) and (6) leave intact a termination when` `terminated under another power of the Commonwealth` IF
    `terminated under another power of the Commonwealth`

§ `16 Rules`

DECLARE `rule matter` IS ONE OF
    `a matter the Act requires or permits to be prescribed`
    `a matter necessary or convenient for carrying out or giving effect to the Act`
    `an offence or civil penalty`
    `a power of arrest or detention`
    `a power of entry, search or seizure`
    `a tax`
    `a direct amendment of the text of the Act`
    `another matter`

-- s 16(1): "The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules prescribing matters: (a)
-- required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed by the rules; or (b) necessary or convenient
-- to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this Act."
-- s 16(2): "To avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following: (a) create an offence or civil
-- penalty; (b) provide powers of: (i) arrest or detention; or (ii) entry, search or seizure;
-- (c) impose a tax; (d) directly amend the text of this Act."
-- Whether a matter is necessary or convenient is a judgment; the caller classifies the matter.
@ref s 16(1), (2)
GIVEN m IS A `rule matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rules may make provision for` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `a matter the Act requires or permits to be prescribed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a matter necessary or convenient for carrying out or giving effect to the Act` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
